Ottid — third-party source notices
===================================

This file lists third-party source code that Ottid's own source files are
derived from, with the notices their licenses require. Third-party material
that is vendored or bundled as-is (fonts, model weights, runtimes) is listed in
NOTICE. Every file named below carries a header comment pointing back here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Coucou
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Origin:  https://github.com/Louis-CFM/coucou
License: MIT (reproduced below)

Ottid's overlay window adapts the windowing mechanics of Coucou's Windows
build: the cursor poll that toggles click-through over the drawn regions, the
display-change check, the cursor and button reads, the damped spring and the
cubic-bezier easing, the hover rules that keep a card open, and the
cursor-following gaze mapping. Each was rewritten for Ottid; no Coucou names,
characters, artwork, icons, sounds, animations or other assets were taken.

Derived files (Ottid path  <-  Coucou path):

  packages/shared-rust/src/overlay/hit_test.rs
      <-  windows/src-tauri/src/island.rs          (click-through decision)
  packages/shared-rust/src/overlay/regions.rs
      <-  windows/src-tauri/src/island.rs          (hit rectangles, generalised)
  packages/shared-rust/src/overlay/pointer.rs
      <-  windows/src-tauri/src/platform/windows.rs (cursor_physical,
                                                     left_button_down)
  packages/shared-rust/src/overlay/gaze.rs
      <-  windows/src/island/island.ts             (eyes follow the cursor)
  apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/overlay.rs
      <-  windows/src-tauri/src/island.rs          (cursor poll, click-through
                                                     toggle, display check)
  apps/desktop/src/lib/motion/spring.ts
      <-  windows/src/core/anim.ts                 (Spring, cubicBezier)
  apps/desktop/src/lib/overlay/island.ts
      <-  windows/src/island/fsm.ts                (IslandStateMachine hover
                                                     rules)

The Claude Code hooks bridge's Windows named-pipe listener adapts the hardened
pipe server of the fork https://github.com/YojoTan/coucou (MIT, under the same
copyright and license file as Coucou): the explicit DACL that admits only the
user's SID, `first_pipe_instance` and `reject_remote_clients`, and a fresh
pipe instance per accepted connection. The protocol, its authentication and
everything else in the bridge are Ottid's own.

  packages/shared-rust/src/agent_bridge/endpoint.rs
      <-  windows/src-tauri/src/pipe.rs            (pipe_sddl,
                                                     create_instance, the
                                                     accept loop)

